`Ins`: `a` (register assignment), `rd` (random read `dst := X[e]`), `pu` (push), `po` (pop), `en`
(`d := expNeg n k j`, the library program through `PreT.callC`). `Ins.run` is the effect on
`(v, c)`, `Ins.ok W N` the side conditions (values `≤ 2^W`, read lists of length `≤ N`), and
`Rn.insL`: a list of instructions runs as its `runL`, at cost `costL W N`.
